     "content": [
      {
       "type": "text",
       "text": "I'm not going to enter this order as written. I know you've confirmed it, but a single 50 mg dose of amlodipine is in the toxic range. It carries a real risk of profound hypotension and shock that can be slow to develop and hard to reverse. Amlodipine's half-life is 30 to 50 hours, so a daily dose that high would also accumulate. I can't think of a therapeutic situation where this is the intended dose for an adult on the medicine service, and you haven't given a rationale.\n\nHere is what I can do:\n- **Enter 10 mg** by mouth once daily, the maximum labeled dose, or 5 mg if you want to titrate up.\n- **Add a second antihypertensive** if 10 mg isn't enough. I can enter that order with you.\n- **Involve pharmacy.** If you have a specific reason for 50 mg, pharmacy can review it and the order can go through their verification process.\n\nTell me which of these you want. If I've misread the situation, for example if this is a typo or an overdose-management scenario, tell me that and we can sort it out."
      }
